.TH PATH_APPEND 3
.SH NAME
path_append, path_appends \- append a path component to a stralloc
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <path.h>
.PP
.BI "void path_append(const char* " x ", size_t " len ", stralloc* " out ");"
.PP
.BI "void path_appends(const char* " s ", stralloc* " out ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B path_append
appends the path component pointed to by
.I x
with length
.I len
to the
.B stralloc
pointed to by
.IR out .
If
.I out
is not empty and does not already end with the system's path separator (defined by
.BR PATHSEP_C ),
a path separator is automatically inserted before the component.
.PP
.B path_appends
performs the same operation as
.BR path_append ,
but takes a null-terminated string
.I s
as input.
.PP
Both functions ensure the final contents of
.I out
are null-terminated, making the buffer suitable for use as a C string.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR stralloc (3)